{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "c13f2079-ed43-845e-86a3-6fec30f8a238",
  "created_at": "2025-12-08T12:21:33-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Sean Cullen",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:10-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:14-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi Tony. Sean Cullen here. Hmm, let me see. I just bought a house, closed a few weeks back, and the first water and sewer bill came in and it's got the old owner's name on it. Not mine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:27-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that happens a lot right after a sale. The bill usually follows the account until the transfer gets processed. Is the amount what's bothering you, or the name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:37-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both, honestly. It's a big number. Way too big for a house I haven't even lived in a month. Now, I've also got the other place, the one I've had for years, so, hmm, wait. Let me look at which one this is. Actually, I think I've got the two bills mixed up here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No rush, take your time. Do you see an account number on the top right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:19:59-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, okay. Hmm. So the one with the old owner's name, that's the new house. The one with my name is the old house. I had them backwards. So this big one is definitely the new house, and it's covering a stretch before I owned it, I'd bet."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:20:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's possible. If the meter reading covers dates before your closing, part of that usage belongs to the seller. Was there a final reading done at the closing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:20:23-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not that I know of. Nobody told me anything about it. I'm not paying for somebody else's water, I'll tell you that. So how do I dispute it? Formally, I mean, in writing or whatever it takes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:20:35-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Best way is a written request to the water division, with your name, the account number, the closing date, and a copy of the settlement statement if you have it. Say you're disputing the charge for the period before you owned it. They'll review the reads and adjust."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:20:50-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Hmm, and do I send it or drop it off? Or, no, never mind, I can bring it in. I'm usually down by the waterfront on a sunny day anyway, long lunch, so City Hall's not far."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:21:02-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, bringing it to the counter works fine. Want me to note your number on the account in case they need to reach you? I have it as 401-555-0172."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:21:12-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the one. And the bill, it's not due yet, is it? I don't want a late fee on top of this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:21:20-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll add a note that it's under dispute. Get the letter in soon and that note will back you up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:21:27-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. Okay. Thanks, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-08T12:21:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it, Mr. Cullen. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
